{
  "$comment": "P4.D376 — the reach differential (v4 `lib/mount-index/reach.ts`, NEW in `0c47f4539`, pin `624d0d25c`). Runs over its OWN copies of the tiered-mount-pool baked pair (the shared builder), after applying `plants` (pre-init, `@vault:<characterId>` params resolved off the main copy first), so the tiered matrix is untouched. `pure` = tier-1 exact (orderMounts / bucketMounts / groupOriginMap over literal pools). The rest is tier-2 over the real DB, in order (an ensure arm mints state the later arms see): resolveOwnerStore (every scope x ensure off / swallow / throw, a planted folder failure via a BEFORE INSERT trigger, archived allow / refuse, R-F's corrupt project + group rows), the R-F read-each-way arms, classifyMount, castGroupMounts, resolveCastPool. A minted store id is masked `<minted>`; the store row, its folders and the owner pointer are dumped. `character` rows are projected to v4's `ReachCharacterRow` keys. Every `[Reach]` line is compared (`error` omitted).",
